course: dictionary
lesson: 11489
title: Afterthought
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An afterthought is something you think of, say or add later, after the main thing is already done. The word is built from after and thought, so it is a thought that comes after the plan.
explain: «We made the cake, and then, as an afterthought, we added cherries on top.» The cherries were not in the plan at the start. They came later, so they were an afterthought.
explain: Sometimes an afterthought is treated as less important, because it was not planned with much care. «The little room at the back was an afterthought, with no proper window.» The builders did not plan it carefully, so it feels less important than the rest of the house.
fact: An afterthought is something you think of, say or add later.
fact: «Afterthought» means something added after the main thing is done, and sometimes without much care.
fact: Useful phrases: «as an afterthought», «an afterthought to», and «no afterthought».
fact: In stories and writing, a sentence added as an afterthought comes at the end, and it shows that it was not planned.
fact: Be careful: calling something an afterthought can sound unkind, because it suggests the thing is not very important.
exercise: «We forgot the milk, so we went back for it as an afterthought.» What is an afterthought here? | *Something added later, after the main plan | Something that was lost forever | A type of cold drink | The main reason for the trip
exercise: «The extra line was added at the end of the story as an afterthought.» Find and copy the word that means something added later. | story | ending | *afterthought | sentence
exercise: «The little side room was an afterthought, built with no care.» What does this suggest? | It was the biggest room in the house | It was planned with great care from the start | *It was added later and treated as less important | It was painted gold
test: «Mum's note was an afterthought, written on the envelope after she had left.» Why was the note written? | *To add something she had forgotten, after the main message | To tell the post office a secret | To copy the letter | To make the envelope heavier
test: Ben says, «I'll bring a drink, as an afterthought.» What does as an afterthought mean? | A kind of cup | Planned months before | *Added later, not planned at the start | Something he will never do
exam: Ruby says, «Her name was an afterthought on the list.» What does she mean? | Her name was crossed out forever | Her name was the first thing on the list | *Her name was added later and not planned with care | Her name was written in gold at the top
